Package: lindesk-telemetry
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Dipankar Sarkar <me@dipankar.name>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: lindesk (= @VERSION@)@SHLIBS_DEPENDS@
Suggests: duckdb
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dipankar/lindesk
Description: telemetry lake for lindesk (DuckDB + Vortex)
 lindesk is a userspace resource governor that keeps the application you are
 using responsive while background work runs. This optional package adds its
 telemetry: pressure, per-unit usage, every decision and its reason, recorded
 into a hive-partitioned Vortex lake and queryable with SQL.
 .
 It contains the telemetry plugin (lindesk-telemetry-sink, loaded by lindeskd
 and lindesk-session, writing at idle I/O priority), lindesk-data (DuckDB:
 query, export, import, compaction, rollups, retention) and its hourly
 maintenance timers. lindeskctl query/data/simulate and lindesk-mcp use it when
 it is installed. Removing it leaves lindesk running without telemetry.
